\ No newline at end of file
+- Movie search with a 500 ms debounce and cancellation of outdated requests.
+- Paginated results, with the page reset when the query or tab changes.
+- Movie posters, release dates, genres, summaries, and community scores.
+- Personal ratings from 0.5 to 10; click the selected rating again to remove it.
+- A **My ratings** tab backed by TMDB.
+- Responsive cards for desktop and mobile, including a fallback for missing or broken posters.
+- Loading, empty, offline, and API error states, with a retry button for failed requests.
+- Search remains available when guest sessions or genre requests fail.
+
+## Stack
+
+Next.js 16 App Router · React 19 · TypeScript · Ant Design 6 · date-fns · TMDB REST API
+
+## Run locally
+
+Requires Node.js 20.9+ and a TMDB API key.
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/VeraI98/movies-app.git
+cd movies-app
+npm ci
+cp .env.example .env.local
+```
+
+Set your key in `.env.local`:
+
+```dotenv
+NEXT_PUBLIC_MOVIEDB_API_KEY=your_tmdb_api_key
+```
+
+Request a key in your [TMDB account settings](https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api). This app uses the API key, rather than the API Read Access Token.
+
+```bash
+npm run dev
+```
+
+Open [localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000).
+
+## Quality checks
+
+```bash
+npm run lint
+npm run typecheck
+npm test
+npm run build
+```
+
+API tests use mocked fetch responses; no credentials or live TMDB access are required.
+
+## Architecture
+
+| Location                         | Responsibility                                                |
+| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `app/page.tsx`                   | Search query, selected tab, and page layout                   |
+| `app/components/Header.tsx`      | Search input and debounced query updates                      |
+| `app/components/MovieList.tsx`   | Fetching, pagination, request cancellation, and result states |
+| `app/components/MovieCard.tsx`   | Movie details, poster fallback, and rating submission         |
+| `app/context/SessionContext.tsx` | Guest session and shared in-memory rating updates             |
+| `app/context/GenreContext.tsx`   | Shared genre dictionary                                       |
+| `app/lib/moviedb.ts`             | Typed TMDB API functions                                      |
+
+## Deployment
+
+Import the repository into Vercel, set `NEXT_PUBLIC_MOVIEDB_API_KEY`, and deploy. Changing a `NEXT_PUBLIC_` variable requires a new build. This variable is included in the browser bundle; do not use this pattern for private server credentials.
+
+The Vercel URL above responded successfully during preparation. Configure the repository homepage to use the same address.
+
+## Limitations
+
+Ratings belong to a temporary TMDB guest session, not a permanent user account. The session is stored in the current browser when local storage is available. TMDB may expire or invalidate it; ratings are unavailable when session creation fails. Ratings already saved on TMDB are displayed when **My ratings** is loaded; in-session changes also appear in search results.
+
+## Portfolio description
+
+> Developed a movie search application with Next.js and TypeScript, integrating the TMDB REST API for movie search, genres, pagination, and guest-session ratings. Implemented debounced search, request cancellation, responsive cards, and loading, empty, offline, and error states.
+
+This is an educational project by [VeraI98](https://github.com/VeraI98).
+
+Movie data and images are provided by [TMDB](https://www.themoviedb.org/). This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.
